        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Xi told the White House dinner that Chinese and American peoples “fought shoulder to shoulder against Japanese militarist aggressors.”\n\nThat line is real. The wartime alliance was real. The Flying Tigers were real. The Hump airlift was real. Chinese civilians really did die saving downed American pilots.\n\nWhat he left out is also real.\n\nThe government Washington allied with was the Republic of China. The army that fought Japan in the big battles was Chiang Kai-shek’s Nationalists, not Mao’s Communists. The PRC did not exist until 1949. Five years after Japan surrendered, Chinese troops were killing Americans in Korea.\n\nA shared enemy makes a good toast. It does not rewrite who carried the war, who took power afterward, or what happened next."
        },
